es", "description": "This module builds directly on euclidean geometry and parametrization and develops curves. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for global curve theory.", "children": [{"id": "446497f3-6f04-4707-bedf-3995f92a8891", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Arc length", "children": [], "description": "Arc length identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within curves. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before curvature because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "171096b6-636a-4731-a331-b9dd5c6bd616", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Curvature", "children": [], "description": "Curvature is a governing quantity in curves, linking local calculations to system-level behavior and offering a consistency check. After arc length, curvature supplies what is needed to address torsion."}, {"id": "9964ddae-582e-4041-af57-0c6091a7adac", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Torsion", "children": [], "description": "Torsion identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within curves. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After curvature, torsion supplies what is needed to address frenet frame."}, {"id": "b935f2e3-fa9b-4fbf-b49d-91454d0e585e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Frenet frame", "children": [], "description": "Frenet frame identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within curves. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After torsion, frenet frame supplies what is needed to address fundamental theorem."}, {"id": "904133e6-48a2-4560-9496-35b8e515c4a9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fundamental theorem", "children": [], "description": "Fundamental theorem provides a formal guarantee or inference rule for curves, allowing later conclusions to be justified rather than inferred from examples alone. As the final topic in this module, fundamental theorem carries the completed idea into global curve theory."}]}, {"id": "525aabef-41ac-4c64-88da-3c74a8c52224", "type": "topic", "title": "Global curve theory", "description": "This module builds directly on curves and develops global curve theory. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for regular surfaces.", "children": [{"id": "04fd3a40-2f94-453d-a665-19c31cc50614", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Winding", "children": [], "description": "Winding identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within global curve theory. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before total curvature because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "3958443b-df24-4d0f-981e-1a889016d4fb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Total curvature", "children": [], "description": "Total curvature is a governing quantity in global curve theory, linking local calculations to system-level behavior and offering a consistency check. After winding, total curvature supplies what is needed to address isoperimetric ideas."}, {"id": "3f415e38-a96a-44a7-bea8-a04a985118f6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Isoperimetric ideas", "children": [], "description": "Isoperimetric ideas identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within global curve theory. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, isoperimetric ideas carries the completed idea into regular surfaces."}]}, {"id": "4ddaae87-0640-44dc-aafa-509f577d6f84", "type": "topic", "title": "Regular surfaces", "description": "This module builds directly on global curve theory and develops regular surfaces. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for tangent spaces and differentials.", "children": [{"id": "0b5c4067-11dc-460c-be59-2146b45744c0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Charts", "children": [], "description": "Charts identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within regular surfaces. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before atlases because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "f145fa40-3e19-42d4-b289-d1e25143f4c4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Atlases", "children": [], "description": "Atlases identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within regular surfaces. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After charts, atlases supplies what is needed to address examples."}, {"id": "7b35f521-a6e1-4a58-b465-c71d47ac219e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Examples", "children": [], "description": "Examples identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within regular surfaces. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After atlases, examples supplies what is needed to address level sets."}, {"id": "964afb2b-1f27-4fe8-9910-fcba0e5aa895", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Level sets", "children": [], "description": "Level sets identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within regular surfaces. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After examples, level sets supplies what is needed to address regular-value viewpoint."}, {"id": "65001b92-ee07-42cf-9ae1-172de1542c91", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Regular-value viewpoint", "children": [], "description": "Regular-value viewpoint identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within regular surfaces. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, regular-value viewpoint carries the completed idea into tangent spaces and differentials."}]}, {"id": "3a4ccaf9-1d66-4698-bc17-77a835fe529b", "type": "topic", "title": "Tangent spaces and differentials", "description": "This module builds directly on regular surfaces and develops tangent spaces and differentials. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for first fundamental form.", "children": [{"id": "59a11165-5599-4176-ba44-37e098a7dab6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Tangent vectors", "children": [], "description": "Tangent vectors identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within tangent spaces and differentials. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before jacobians because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "55befcf6-bbad-4174-8e05-83b91204f5e0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Jacobians", "children": [], "description": "Jacobians identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within tangent spaces and differentials. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After tangent vectors, jacobians supplies what is needed to address pushforward."}, {"id": "b159e54d-df4b-4f62-999c-5f6e8817c804", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pushforward", "children": [], "description": "Pushforward identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within tangent spaces and differentials. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After jacobians, pushforward supplies what is needed to address gradients."}, {"id": "bd8402b8-a805-4c46-bb7d-f9f9b2b4c46f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Gradients", "children": [], "description": "Gradients identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within tangent spaces and differentials. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, gradients carries the completed idea into first fundamental form."}]}, {"id": "52198229-be9a-4634-90bc-c35523b182ef", "type": "topic", "title": "First fundamental form", "description": "This modul